        "branch": "whole",
        "query": "We have a monorepo called \"Meridian\" for a cross-platform health journaling app (iOS via SwiftUI, Android via Jetpack Compose, shared Kotlin Multiplatform modules, and a Node.js BFF layer). I need three things done: (1) Review our main journal entry composition views on both platforms — check accessibility labels, VoiceOver/TalkBack support, layout consistency between iOS and Android, test coverage of the view models, and auto-create tickets for any critical issues you find. (2) Generate nested AGENTS.md coding guidelines for each module in the monorepo — detect the languages and tooling per module, ask me about our architecture preferences, and set up Spotless for our Kotlin/JVM modules plus any missing linters for the Swift and Node layers. (3) We're also designing a \"Reflection Spaces\" feature where users navigate between different journaling modalities (gratitude, dream log, mood tracking, free-write) and we want the navigation graph to enforce that you can only transition between spaces whose \"emotional distance\" satisfies triangle inequality constraints — essentially treating each modality as a node in a mathematical possibility space where valid paths correspond to truth procedures over the user's journaling history events. We want the transition logic to use Badiou-inspired event ontology so that a new modality only \"appears\" as reachable when a genuine journaling event breaks the current situation. Can you architect that navigation model, review the existing views, and get the AGENTS.md guidelines scaffolded all in one pass?",
